# build output
/bin/

# Encoder output, regenerable bit-for-bit by `make convert` and `make
# corpus-bench` (verified: deleting both and re-running reproduces every file
# identically). Tracking them meant 6.3 MiB of the 7.4 MiB tree, and every
# encoder change rewrote all 36 files, which buries the actual diff on a branch
# that is supposed to be reviewable.
#
# The measurement record is docs/*.md and that IS tracked: the point of the
# project is turning "I improved it a bit" into "I improved it by X% on the
# corpus", and that claim lives in the generated report, not in the artefacts
# that produced it.
/assets/svg/
/testdata/corpus/.trace/

